{"id":"G0649","lemma":"ἀποστέλλω","transliteration":"apostellō","sayIt":"apostellō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to send","meaning":"ἀπο-στέλλω,\n[in LXX very freq., almost always for שׁלח ;]\nprop., to send away, to dispatch on service;\n1. to send with a commission, or on service;\n(a) of persons: Christ, Mat.10:40; the apostles, 10:16; servants, Mrk.12:2; angels, 13:27;\n(b) of things: ὄνος, Mat.21:3; τὸ δρέπανον, Mrk.4:29; τ. λόγον, Act.10:36; τ. ἐπαγγελίαν (i.e. the promised Holy Spirit), Luk.24:49, Rec.; before εἰς, Mat.20:2, Luk.11:49, Jhn.3:17; ὀπίσω, Luk.19:14; ἔμπροσθεν, Jhn.3:28; πρὸ προσώπου, Mat.11:10; πρός, Mat.21:34; with ref. to sender or place of departure: ἀπό, Luk.1:26 (Rec. ὑπό); παρά, Jhn.1:6; ἐκ, ib. 1:19; ὑπό, Act.10:17 (Rec. ἀπό); before inf., Mrk.3:14, al.; ἵνα, Mrk.12:2, al.; εἰς (of purpose), Heb.1:14; without direct obj.: before πρός, Jhn.5:33; λέγων, Jhn.11:3; ἀποστείλας, with indic., Mat.2:16, Act.7:14, Rev.1:1.\n2. to send away, dismiss: Luk.4:18, Mrk.5:10 8:26 12:3 (cf. ἐξ-, συν-αποστέλλω).\nSYN.: πέμπω, the general term. ἀ. \"suggests official or authoritative sending\" (see Thayer, see word πέμπω; Westc., Jo., 298; Epp. Jo., 125; Cremer, 529; MM, see word). (AS)","glosses":["sent","send","has sent","sent out","have sent","send out"],"count":130,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-2","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"Sending orders","kjv":"sent forth"}},{"chapterId":"mat-8","v":31,"renderings":{"bsb":"send us"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"sent out","kjv":"sent forth"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"am sending you out","kjv":"send"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":40,"renderings":{"bsb":"sent","kjv":"him that sent"}},{"chapterId":"mat-11","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"will send","kjv":"send"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":41,"renderings":{"bsb":"will send out","kjv":"shall send forth"}},{"chapterId":"mat-14","v":35,"renderings":{"bsb":"they sent word","kjv":"they sent out"}},{"chapterId":"ma